  ('156567391266704074', 'Hoard', 2024, 'Drama, Romance, Fantasy', 'Luna Carmoon, Nanu Segal, Ina Lüders', 'Luna Carmoon', 'Saura Lightfoot Leon, Joseph Quinn, Hayley Squires, Lily-Beau Leach, Deba Hekmat, Samantha Spiro, Cathy Tyson, Nabil Elouahabi', null, 'The story follows Maria – a teenager whose mother used to be a hoarder. Now (set in the 90s) she lives in a foster home where a previous resident, Michael, inspires her to revisit the childhood memories and passions that she has repressed.', 'The story follows Maria – a teenager whose mother used to be a hoarder. Now (set in the 90s) she lives in a foster home where a previous resident, Michael, inspires her to revisit the childhood memories and passions that she has repressed.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/81VQOyGSnyMxE2SWf0bgnHAAKeT.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:996087'),
  ('403403599316063563', 'Hobgoblins', 1988, 'Horror, Comedy, Science Fiction', 'Rick Sloane, Rick Sloane', 'Rick Sloane', 'Tom Bartlett, Paige Sullivan, Steven Boggs, Kelley Palmer, Billy Frank, Tamara Clatterbuck, Duane Whitaker, James R. Sweeney', 'R', 'A group of hobgoblins, who allow you to live out your fantasies but kill you in the process, escape from a studio vault, and a security guard and his friends must stop them before dawn.', 'A group of hobgoblins, who allow you to live out your fantasies but kill you in the process, escape from a studio vault, and a security guard and his friends must stop them before dawn.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rwSVqMihUeRQR94UxWkGnRbn2ZJ.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:31245'),
  ('1072092066211265054', 'Hobo', 1992, 'Documentary', 'John T. Davis', null, 'Beargrease, Scott Caribou, Minot Louis, Big Red, Duffy', null, 'John T. Davis stashes a camera in his bedroll, catches out, and rides the rails from Minneapolis to Seattle with Beargrease - a part-time hobo and full time philosopher, who narrates their way through the incredible scenery of the Northwest and gives us his views on life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness. Along the way, the pair meet with several other men living life on the margins.', 'John T. Davis stashes a camera in his bedroll, catches out, and rides the rails from Minneapolis to Seattle with Beargrease - a part-time hobo and full time philosopher, who narrates their way through the incredible scenery of the Northwest and gives us his views on life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness. Along the way, the pair meet with several other men living life on the margins.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/yy1nDLlCQj6Lf7iejn2fwf2zPOt.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:138569'),
  ('630128093678565902', 'Hobo with a Shotgun', 2011, 'Crime, Action, Thriller', 'Jason Eisener, Rob Cotterill, Jason Shipley', 'John Davies', 'Rutger Hauer, Molly Dunsworth, Gregory Smith, Robb Wells, Brian Downey, Nick Bateman, Peter Simas, Pasha Ebrahimi', 'NR', 'A vigilante homeless man pulls into a new city and finds himself trapped in urban chaos, a city where crime rules and where the city''s crime boss reigns. Seeing an urban landscape filled with armed robbers, corrupt cops, abused prostitutes and even a pedophile Santa, the Hobo goes about bringing justice to the city the best way he knows how - with a 20-gauge shotgun. Mayhem ensues when he tries to make things better for the future generation. Street justice will indeed prevail.', 'A vigilante homeless man pulls into a new city and finds himself trapped in urban chaos, a city where crime rules and where the city''s crime boss reigns. Seeing an urban landscape filled with armed robbers, corrupt cops, abused prostitutes and even a pedophile Santa, the Hobo goes about bringing justice to the city the best way he knows how - with a 20-gauge shotgun. Mayhem ensues when he tries to make things better for the future generation. Street justice will indeed prevail.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/xxMaO7VoN2BnZit79PedVHnTjcO.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:49010'),
  ('636420277312247356', 'Hobson''s Choice', 1954, 'Comedy, Drama, Romance', 'David Lean, Jack Hildyard, Adrian Pryce-Jones', 'Wynyard Browne, David Lean, Norman Spencer', 'Charles Laughton, John Mills, Brenda De Banzie, Daphne Anderson, Prunella Scales, Richard Wattis, Derek Blomfield, Helen Haye', 'NR', 'A widower refuses to let his three daughters marry in order to avoid paying settlements, so they''ll just have to outsmart him.', 'A widower refuses to let his three daughters marry in order to avoid paying settlements, so they''ll just have to outsmart him.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kbP7EgoiOw2bIypai50JWRsqP7p.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:16410'),
